# FINAL WORDS

I wonder how long it took you to find this.

You followed the photograph.

You found the place.

You found the date.

And eventually, you realized that the face was never the answer.

Suguru Geto is dead.

That much was never in question.

The body, however, remained useful.

People are so easily deceived by what they recognize. A familiar face. A familiar voice. A familiar name.

They see what they expect to see.

Perhaps that is why you are reading this now.

You wanted to know who was standing in Shibuya that night.

You already know the answer.

You have known it since the beginning.

The body was Geto's.

The face was Geto's.

The name was not.

**Kenjaku.**

Remember that name.

It has survived far longer than any body ever could.

---

If this archive survives, then perhaps someone will eventually understand what happened.

If it doesn't, then none of this mattered.

Either way, my work is finished.

Good job I guess.

You need this. 

